    "description": "Static, manually-curated economic calendar. Dates sourced from each institution's own published schedule — original 10 events sourced 2026-09-07; EIA Weekly Petroleum Status Report and USDA WASDE/Grain Stocks/Crop Production entries added 2026-09-27 from eia.gov's release schedule and NASS's 2026 Agricultural Statistics Board Calendar — not guessed, not from a paid calendar API. EIA/USDA entries extended through 2026-12-16 on 2026-10-17, sourced from eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/schedule.php (whose own holiday-exceptions list for the rest of 2026 is only the Oct 9 week — shifted to Thu Oct 15 — and the Nov 6 week — shifted to Thu Nov 12 for Veterans Day; Thanksgiving week is not listed as shifted), USDA/NASS's own 2026-NASS-PFEI-Schedule.pdf (data.nass.usda.gov) for Crop Production (Nov 10, Dec 10 — confirmed from that PDF's own NOV/DEC columns), and the WASDE report's usda.gov schedule page (also Nov 10, Dec 10, released same day as Crop Production as usual). No USDA Grain Stocks entry was added for this window — NASS's own PFEI PDF shows '--' (no release) for both November and December 2026; its next release is January 2027, outside this window. Each EIA row also carries a visible creditLine, 'Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration', rendered on the calendar page. On 2026-10-27, added FOMC (Dec 9), ECB Governing Council (Dec 17), and BOJ Monetary Policy Meeting (Dec 18) rows read directly off each bank's own calendar page; US Employment Situation and Consumer Price Index rows for November 2026, December 2026, and January 2027 read off bls.gov's own monthly schedule pages (day numbers printed on each page, cross-checked across both the source month's page and the following month's page where it repeated the same entry); and a tentative OPEC+ seven-countries row for Nov 1, 2026 — opec.org's press-release page would not load (HTTP 402), so this one row is sourced from a news report of OPEC's own Oct 4 statement instead and is marked tentative pending confirmation on opec.org. See docs/brain/09_BACKLOG.md and docs/brain/LIVE_TODO.md for the sourcing note and the live-provider upgrade path (e.g. Trading Economics) if this ever needs to become dynamic. On 2026-11-09, added scheduleStatus/lastCheckedAt to every row; re-verified the OPEC+ Nov 1 row directly against opec.org's own pr-detail page (it occurred as reported, now scheduleStatus:confirmed, sourceUrl/sourceLabel updated) and added its already-announced follow-up meeting (opec.org, Nov 29); added UK ONS GDP monthly estimate (ons.gov.uk, confirmed, Nov 12), Australia ABS CPI October 2026 data (abs.gov.au, confirmed, Nov 25 — matches the ABS page's own 'Next Release 25/11/2026' listing), India RBI MPC decision (rbi.org.in prid=62422, confirmed Dec 2–4, 2026 — RBI's own schedule page, not the Dec 6–8 date floated elsewhere), and IEA Oil Market Report November + December 2026 editions (iea.org's own OMR data-product page, confirmed). China NBS's release calendar (stats.gov.cn) could not be verified — both the English and Chinese pages timed out on every fetch attempt from this environment on 2026-11-09 — so no NBS row was added; see docs/brain/LIVE_TODO.md.",
    "sourcedAt": "2026-11-09",
